  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/fmo#DiagonalCrack">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/dot#StructuralDamage"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/fmo#Crack"/>
    <rdfs:label>Diagonal crack</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Crack with diagonal progression.</rdfs:comment>
    <ns3:hasCausation rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/fmo#InPlaneFailure"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n49030e428ac1404292800e1d33196617b236">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#Imp"/>
    <rdfs:label>Vertical bending</rdfs:label>
    <ns2:isRuleEnabled rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ns2:isRuleEnabled>
    <rdfs:comment>If a masonry wall has a vulnerability that is ‘excessive slenderness’  and has a vulnerability that is ‘presence of horizontal thrusts’, and has a vulnerability that is ‘deformable floor, and it has a behaviour that is ‘inadequate out of plane behaviour’, then it has an occurring mechanism that is ‘vertical bending’.</rdfs:comment>
    <ns1:body rdf:nodeID="n49030e428ac1404292800e1d33196617b237"/>
    <ns1:head rdf:nodeID="n49030e428ac1404292800e1d33196617b245"/>
  </rdf:Description>
